__pycache__/
*.pyc
site/
.DS_Store

# Source documents are not redistributed -- see data/README.md. Citations
# (including DOIs) live in subjects/<slug>/sources.json instead.
#
# Both formats, for the same reason. data/<slug>.txt is the text extracted
# from a source we obtained legitimately, but extraction changes the format,
# not the copyright: "open access" spans everything from CC-BY (redistributable
# with attribution) to free-to-read-only (not redistributable), and this
# pipeline records no license field to tell them apart. Keeping the text
# locally is what makes grounding re-checkable; publishing it is a separate
# act needing per-source license evidence we do not currently collect.
data/*.pdf
data/*.txt

# Source-discovery tool: kept private/local for now (unproven, and
# specifically about finding copyright-adjacent material) -- see
# the "Visibility" decision in the sourcing-plan discussion.
scripts/find_sources.py
candidates.json
.find_sources_cache.json*
.find_sources_dismissed.json

# Same discovery pipeline, extended to download PDFs and run continuously
# and unattended (see source-discovery-plan.md) -- same private/local
# reasoning as find_sources.py above; only build_site.py's writes into
# subjects/ are the public, committed output of any of this.
scripts/download_sources.py
scripts/run_pipeline.py
scripts/test_api_access.py
scripts/check_scope.py
HANDOFF.md
PIPELINE_GUIDE.md
pipeline_state.json
pipeline_log.txt
.pipeline_manifest.json
candidates_bootstrap.json
candidates_autoseed.json
.related_fields_scratch.json
data/_pending/
.scope_verdict_scratch.json
data/_additional/
scripts/pipeline_status.py

# Local backups of the gitignored pipeline files above -- same contents, same
# reasons; a .bak of an ignored file is still that file.
materials_taxonomy.json.*
pipeline_state.json.*
.openalex_backlog.json
scripts/backup_evidence.py

# Domain taxonomies are tracked once their run has converged -- they are field maps,
# not credentials or copyrighted text, and they are what makes the corpus
# reproducible. A taxonomy is left ignored while its run is still growing it, so a
# half-grown state never lands in a commit; remove its line here once that run
# reports "run to completion".
#   tracked: chemistry_history_taxonomy.json, materials_taxonomy.json, physics_taxonomy.json,
#            cs_taxonomy.json

# Per-domain pipeline state -- bookkeeping, never useful outside this machine.
pipeline_state.json
chemistry_state.json
physics_state.json
cs_state.json

# Working notes, not a project artifact.
working-taxonomy-of-science.docx
cs_state.json

# Wikidata lookup cache for scripts/geocode_places.py -- rebuildable, and large.
.geocode_cache.json
